      "value": "I already know what the VRChat Devs would say:\n\n# **Con to adding free market:**\n\nAllowing free avatars = many low quality avatars flood the market\n\n# **Fix:**\n\nA simple \"sort by price\" or \"show/hide free avatars\" or \"browse verified market vs browse free market\" option will allow players to choose if they want to browse the paid or free market.\n\n# **Pros:**\n\nThe devs already know the majority of the playerbase wants to find good quality avatars without having to learn unity.\n\nThis will certainly be used by everyone to great extent.\n\nGiving players a good FREE experience will retain those players. More retained players = bigger market and eventuality of sales.\n\n# **Cons of current non-free market:**\n\nHowever, imagine the new player experience when they join VRChat, and think, \"Wow, to get a GOOD quality avatar, I have to pay money, otherwise I am stuck with poor avatars?\"\n\nThat is a bad new player experience. VRChat cannot force people who are  unable to buy to somehow have money to buy.\n\nSo, by not including free options, those players are just alienated instead.\n\n# **Fix:**\n\nThe solution for that is just as Nekosan suggested :)\n\n# **Pros:**\n\nGiving players a good FREE experience will retain those players. More retained players = bigger market and eventuality of sales.\n\n# **Con to adding free market:**\n\nAllowing free avatars - it will be hard to navigate and find good quality avatars\n\n# **Note:**\n\nThis is already partially solved, because as VRChat intends, the paid market will be a place for high quality models curated by creators VRChat has chosen.\n\nHowever, the problem would still exist in the scope of the free market only.\n\n# **Fix:**\n\nJust as any other site does, giving players statistics like \"how many times favorited\" or \"how many people currently using this avatar\" or a like/dislike count/ratio, will help players sort.\n\nAdditionally, we already have avatar reporting. And VRChat I believe is already restricting the new market to avatars using up-to-date unity and SDK.\n\nHaving the option is better than not.\n\nWe essentially already have a free (and paid) market, just not a good way to navigate it.\n\n# **Pros:**\n\nGoodbye Prismic's Avatar Search\n\n# **Cons:**\n\nGoodbye Prismic's Avatar Search",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
